\section{Alabaster format, \code{AlabasterParam}}{


\code{saveMsObject()} with an \code{AlabasterParam()} stores the backend to a stash
folder in \emph{alabaster} format. Individual components of the backend are
stored using base functionality of the \emph{alabaster.base} Bioconductor package
into specific sub-folders within the main stash directory. These are:
\itemize{
\item \emph{dbinfo} directory: contains a \code{data.frame} saved with \emph{alabaster.base}
with the database-specific information such as database name, host etc.
\item \emph{spectra_ids} directory: contains an \code{integer} vector saved with
\emph{alabaster.base} with the IDs (indices) of the individual spectra.
}

The remaining directories hold the content of the \code{MsBackendCached} object
the \code{MsBackendOfflineSql} extends (i.e., all locally cached data). Using
parameter \code{consolidate = TRUE} will also store the database file within
the folder (if supported).

In addition to the \code{saveMsObject()} and \code{readMsObject()} also the
\emph{alabaster.base} \code{saveObject()} and \code{readObject()} methods are directly
supported.
}

\section{Text-file format, \code{PlainTextParam}}{


\code{saveMsObject()} with a \code{PlainTextParam} stores the content of a
\code{MsBackendOfflineSql} as text files into the stash folder. This creates
two text files:
\itemize{
\item \emph{ms_backend_dbinfo.txt}: a two-column tabulator delimited text file with
columns \code{"key"} and \code{"value"} (first line being the header) with each
row representing a key-value pair with the SQL database connection
information. This includes \code{"dbname"} (the name of the database - for
SQLite databases the SQLite database file name), \code{"dbdriver"} the database
driver class (e.g. \code{"RSQLite::SQLiteDriver"} for SQLite databases),
\code{"user"} with the database user, \code{"host"} with the host running the
database and \code{"port"} with the respective port.
\item \emph{ms_backend_spectra_ids.txt}: a single column text file (first row being
the \emph{header} of the table) with the spectrum identifiers (of
type \code{integer}).
}

Remaining content, such as eventually present locally cached data, are
stored through the \code{saveMsObject()} function of the parent \code{MsBackendCached}
object (see \link{MsBackendCachedStash} for details).
